#: ../../source/templates_cal.md:183
msgid ""
"Cal.com's shadow system is the most sophisticated element of the design —"
" 11 shadow definitions using a multi-layered compositing technique:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_cal.md:184
msgid ""
"**Ring borders**: `0px 0px 0px 1px` shadows act as borders, avoiding CSS "
"`border` entirely. This creates hairline containment without affecting "
"layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_cal.md:185
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Diffused soft shadows**: `0px 4px 8px` at 5% opacity add gentle ambient"
" depth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_cal.md:186
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Sharp contact shadows**: `0px 1px 5px -4px` at 70% opacity create tight"
" bottom-edge shadows for grounding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_cal.md:187
msgid ""
"**Inset highlights**: White inset shadows at the top of buttons create a "
"subtle 3D bevel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_cal.md:188
msgid ""
"Shadows are composed in comma-separated stacks — each surface gets 2-3 "
"layered shadow definitions working together"
msgstr ""

